    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112435" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρύνη</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>toad,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				530b34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Timae.
				156
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				17.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βατράχιον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cyran.
				39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> nickname
			of several Athenian courtesans, from their complexion, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1101
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Macho
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				13.583b
			</span></i>:—so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρῦνις</span></b> , ὁ, name of a Com. Poet,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				971
			</span></i>. (Cf. Skt. <i>babhrús</i> 'brown', OHG.
				<i>brūn</i> 'brown', etc.)</div>
